            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The last decade has contributed to the emergence of telemedicine. Legislation and regulations, new tools, efficient networks and regional deployments have all played their part in its growth. There are several regional solutions, often experimental. The implementation of telemedicine services nevertheless comes up against obstacles which concern all specialities, including cardiology.</AbstractText>
